  "notes": "1990s/2000s club-music idol pop, and the research calls the rhythmic grammar the transferable parameter, so this model is built from the drums out. The class is straight: \"the garage feel is 2-step — kick displaced off the grid with the snare on 2&4 — rather than four-on-the-floor\", so `halfTime` is false at `backbeat_24` with the kick carrying the displacement instead: `syncopation` 0.68 and `offbeat8thShare` 0.44 are the highest in this section, over a `beatSkipProb` that takes beat 1 away. \"UK-garage shuffled 16ths\" is `swing.amount` 0.58 on a 16th grid, and \"Jersey/Baltimore-club triplet kick clusters\" is `tresilloBias` 0.4 with a `16T` roll vocabulary. \"Percussion is mixed soft and dry rather than clipped\" is the quiet velocity tier table and the negative perc gain — the club grammar here is played soft, which is what separates it from every other club-derived model in the roster. No `bass808` block: \"rounded sub-bass and warm synth bass on roots, low in the mix relative to the percussion; no 808 glide vocabulary\", so the bassline is a root-following line at a low register and the parent's explicit null stands. Harmony is \"major-mode and modal loops with mellow maj7/9 voicings\", which is the lowest `triad` share in this batch. The vocal production rules are documented as explicit rules and they drive the melody and counter: recorded without guide vocals, \"no high-pitched belting and no inserted rap section\", and \"sung largely in unison or close octaves by the whole group rather than in a lead-plus-harmony split\" — so `octaveJumpProb` is capped low, the register ceiling stays under the belt, and the counter is `octave_echo` at a high density. \"Hooks are short and repeated conversationally\" is the 1-bar phrase. The arrangement stays flat by design: no big final chorus, short sections. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against the research's high-medium rating; every drum probability, `swing.amount` 0.58, the humanize numbers and `bpm.mode` 135 (the midpoint of the first-named 130—140 garage/Jersey band) are INFERRED.",
